WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.960
Lotline turns a chosen xStocks split into an exact
plan for the next USDC contribution.

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.840
The current release supports 10 assets per plan,
with 832 identities in its bundled Example catalog.

3
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.060
This walkthrough uses the real application, and
clearly labeled synthetic estimates.

4
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.460
The calculation boundary is explicit.

5
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.920
USDC is parsed into integer microunits and
percentages into basis points.

6
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:31.300
Big integer arithmetic calculates each allocation,
then the largest remainder method distributes
leftover microunits deterministically.

7
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.560
The total always matches the entered budget.

8
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.440
Invalid percentage fields never produce a complete
allocation badge.

9
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.880
Example is isolated from Live providers.

10
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.580
The original six practice assets keep their
fixtures.

11
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.620
Additional identities use zero illustrative holdings
and a generic unit estimate.

12
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:54.080
The catalog includes pinned decimals and official
logo assets, while unsupported saved mints remain
visible for repair instead of silently replacing a
user's draft.

13
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.260
Live has a separate verification path.

14
00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.120
Issuer metadata identifies each asset, then Solana
account checks verify its mint and token program.

15
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.080
Token-2022 scaled UI

16
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.380
Amounts require the current mint configuration and
chain time.

17
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.540
Raw holdings and quote outputs go through that
conversion before display.

18
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.880
Decimal formatting alone would be incorrect.

19
00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.620
The server requests amount specific Jupiter quotes
in bounded batches of 3.

20
00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.460
It requests no transaction and supplies no signing
wallet.

21
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.420
Each result keeps its own retrieval time and expiry.

22
00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.680
With a 30 second maximum freshness window.

23
00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.060
Later batches cannot refresh earlier quotes.

24
00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.180
Provider failures and missing routes remain explicit
states.

25
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:44.480
Copy and CSV exports preserve exact allocations,
verified mints, quote sources, and expiry.

26
00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:49.280
An export records whether an estimate was fresh or
stale when exported.

27
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.900
Copying never renews a quote.

28
00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:58.280
Editing the budget or percentages clears estimates
so amounts cannot reuse a mismatched result.

29
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:01.780
Device drafts keep the contribution budget and
split.

30
00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:09.100
Signed in users can explicitly save named plans
through Supabase, protected by row level security.

31
00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.220
Public offline caching excludes private account and
API responses.

32
00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:19.620
Example calculations work offline, while Live
estimates require a connection.

33
00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:24.100
Email delivery remains disabled until a custom
sender is configured.

34
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.040
The responsive web app is installable on supported
mobile and desktop browsers.

35
00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.500
It is a contribution planner, not a broker or
automatic trader.

36
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.960
Users review any purchase independently on Jupiter.

37
00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.260
Lotline makes the numerical plan repeatable and its
Live assumptions inspectable.

